  "description": "Qualitative current and voltage versus a single common time axis for an ideal ohmic resistance, with zero phase difference. No numerical scale, units, period marker, or amplitude value is given. The taller thin voltage curve and shorter thick current curve are separately scaled physical quantities, not numerical comparisons of volts and amperes. Modern regularization uses smooth cosines with one common phase, visible initial maxima and the same sequence of three zero crossings, a negative trough and another positive maximum. It preserves the source unequal right-hand truncations on the falling negative branch without adding a new cycle. Canvas coordinates and amplitude-height ratio are graphical choices, not inferred physical values."
